<DocLayout title="Acknowledgments - SideWave" description="The models and open-source code SideWave uses, and their licenses.">

  <h1>Acknowledgments</h1>
  <p class="doc-lead">SideWave runs on models and code that other people published. This page lists each one, what SideWave uses it for, and its license. The app has the same list in Settings &gt; About &gt; Acknowledgments, with every license and notice file in full.</p>

  <h2>Speech models</h2>
  <p>FluidInference converted these to Core ML so they run on the Neural Engine. The conversions don't retrain or change the models.</p>

  <h3>NVIDIA Parakeet TDT v3 (0.6B)</h3>
  <p>Confirms what you said, one segment at a time. By NVIDIA, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC-BY-4.0</a>. <a href="https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3">Model card</a>.</p>

  <h3>NVIDIA Parakeet Realtime EOU 120M</h3>
  <p>Writes the gray live draft and notices when you stop talking. By NVIDIA, licensed under the <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-license/">NVIDIA Open Model License</a>. <a href="https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet_realtime_eou_120m-v1">Model card</a>.</p>

  <h3>Parakeet Ultra</h3>
  <p>An optional recognition model, post-trained by Moondream from NVIDIA Parakeet. Licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC-BY-4.0</a>. <a href="https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/parakeet-ultra-coreml">Model card</a>.</p>

  <h3>NVIDIA Parakeet TDT v2 (0.6B)</h3>
  <p>An optional English-only recognition model. By NVIDIA, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC-BY-4.0</a>. <a href="https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2">Model card</a>.</p>

  <h3>NVIDIA Parakeet TDT-CTC 110M</h3>
  <p>Checks finished segments against your glossary terms. By NVIDIA, licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC-BY-4.0</a>. <a href="https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt_ctc-110m">Model card</a>.</p>

  <h3>NVIDIA Parakeet Unified EN 0.6B</h3>
  <p>The live transcript during a meeting, on Macs with 16 GB of memory or more. Downloaded only when you ask for it. By NVIDIA, licensed under the <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-license/">NVIDIA Open Model License</a>. <a href="https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-unified-en-0.6b">Model card</a>.</p>

  <h3>NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Diarization</h3>
  <p>Labels up to eight speakers in a meeting. By NVIDIA, licensed under OpenMDW-1.1. <a href="https://huggingface.co/FluidInference/nemotron-3-diarization-coreml">Model card and license</a>.</p>

  <h3>Silero VAD v6</h3>
  <p>Finds where speech starts and stops. By the Silero team, licensed under <a href="https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad/blob/master/LICENSE">MIT</a>. <a href="https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad">Source</a>.</p>

  <h2>Language models</h2>

  <h3>Gemma 4 (E2B, E4B, and 12B)</h3>
  <p>Refine, document edits, vocabulary suggestions, and meeting notes. By Google DeepMind, licensed under <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/core/model_card_4">Apache 2.0</a>. SideWave downloads the 4-bit MLX conversions from <a href="https://huggingface.co/mlx-community">mlx-community</a> when you pick one.</p>

  <h3>Apple Foundation Models</h3>
  <p>Refine on Macs with Apple Intelligence turned on. The model comes with macOS 26 and later, and SideWave calls it through the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundationmodels">Foundation Models framework</a>. SideWave downloads nothing for it.</p>

