  <p>Those projects bring in smaller packages: Apple's Swift Collections, Swift Numerics, Swift Atomics, SwiftNIO, and Swift Crypto (all Apache 2.0), plus <a href="https://github.com/ibireme/yyjson">yyjson</a> and <a href="https://github.com/mattt/EventSource">EventSource</a> (both MIT). MLX Swift includes MLX, MLX C, {'{fmt}'}, and JSON for Modern C++ (all MIT) and Apple's metal-cpp (Apache 2.0). FluidAudio includes fastcluster (BSD), VBx (Apache 2.0), and its Kokoro text front ends, each with its own notice. Swift Syntax is used only while building, and Swift System and Swift ASN.1 are resolved but not linked.</p>

  <h2>Apple frameworks</h2>
  <p>SideWave is written in Swift with SwiftUI. It uses Core ML for the speech models, AVFoundation for audio, and AppKit for the shortcut, the floating preview, and pasting.</p>

  <h2>Something missing?</h2>
  <p>If an attribution here is wrong or missing, <a href="https://github.com/RichardStoker-USDA/SideWave/issues">open an issue</a> and I'll fix it.</p>

